<section class="three-tool-knowledge" id="packing-deep-guide"><h2>Umrah and Hajj Packing List: complete practical, health and ihram guide</h2><p><strong>Short answer:</strong> A useful Umrah or Hajj packing list covers travel documents, appropriate clothing, ihram-related essentials, medicines, hydration and communication. The printable checklist is a <strong>personal preparation aid</strong>; Saudi entry rules, authorised operators, visas and medical requirements must be checked against official current information.</p><nav class="three-tool-nav" aria-label="Guide sections"><a href="#packing-deep-difference">How Umrah packing differs</a><a href="#packing-deep-documents">Passport, visa, permits a</a><a href="#packing-deep-ihram">What clothing and toiletr</a><a href="#packing-deep-health">Medication, accessibility</a><a href="#packing-deep-steps">How to use the printable </a><a href="#packing-deep-sources">Sources</a></nav><div class="three-tool-facts"><div><strong>Checklist: private to device</strong></div><div><strong>Journey: Umrah or Hajj</strong></div><div><strong>Format: printable and CSV</strong></div></div><section class="three-tool-section" id="packing-deep-difference"><h3>How Umrah packing differs from Hajj preparation</h3><p>Umrah can be undertaken outside the specific Hajj days subject to permits and travel rules; Hajj involves additional stages, locations, travel arrangements and official authorisation. Neither journey can be planned safely from a generic shopping list alone. Use your trip mode to organise personal belongings, while relying on official services for the legal itinerary.</p></section>
<section class="three-tool-section" id="packing-deep-documents"><h3>Passport, visa, permits and current Nusuk rules</h3><p>Check passport validity, eligible visa or pilgrimage authorisation, booking documents, accommodation, emergency contacts and insurance appropriate for travel. The official Nusuk Umrah platform describes Ministry-supervised services. Entry procedures, national eligibility and restrictions can change; do not assume a screenshot or an earlier visit's visa policy remains valid.</p></section>
<section class="three-tool-section" id="packing-deep-ihram"><h3>What clothing and toiletries to pack for ihram</h3><p>The state of ihram has specific rules, including distinctions for men and women, fragrances and grooming. Items commonly prepared include suitable clothing or ihram garments, comfortable permitted footwear, personal-care products chosen for the occasion and a secure bag. A travel checklist cannot decide whether a particular garment or scent is permitted under your school.</p></section>
<section class="three-tool-section" id="packing-deep-health"><h3>Medication, accessibility, heat and hydration</h3><p>Plan prescription medicines and their documentation, current vaccination advice, accessible accommodation, suitable walking support, heat protection and safe hydration. Pilgrimage crowds, long distances and climate can create serious practical demands. Travellers with mobility restrictions should make an individual plan with medical and authorised pilgrimage providers rather than relying on a checklist as medical advice.</p></section>
<section class="three-tool-section" id="packing-deep-steps"><h3>How to use the printable Umrah packing checklist</h3><p>Select Umrah or Hajj, review the grouped categories, tick only items actually prepared, and print or export CSV. The list saves your existing checked items in the current browser. Before leaving, compare the personal list with the operator's required documentation and official medical, airline and Saudi entry instructions. Reset the ticks only when starting a new preparation cycle.</p></section>
<section class="three-tool-section" id="packing-deep-example"><h3>Worked example: preparing a small carry-on bag</h3><p>For a short Umrah trip, a traveller may allocate a carry-on section to travel documents, phone/charging, required medicine, contacts and a suitable water bottle if allowed by airline security. A separate bag can hold clothing and toiletries suited to ihram. What is permissible during ihram and on the plane needs separate checking; no list can guarantee airport or religious acceptance.</p></section>
<section class="three-tool-section" id="packing-deep-privacy"><h3>Where the packing list stores your progress</h3><p>The checklist uses an existing local storage key so older checkmarks remain available after this upgrade. Exported CSV contains the item text and whether it was ticked; it does not submit passport details, booking numbers or medical information to a server. The browser's data may be lost if the device is changed or storage is cleared.</p></section>
<section class="three-tool-section" id="packing-deep-warnings"><h3>Common packing mistakes before Hajj and Umrah</h3><p>Do not assume tickets alone provide a valid permit, take medicines without checking rules, bring prohibited goods, wear fragranced products during a restricted state without advice, or overlook journey safety and hydration. Verify official current Nusuk or Ministry instructions and a qualified guide's Umrah/Hajj rites before departure.</p></section><section class="three-tool-section" id="packing-deep-faq"><h3>Frequently asked questions</h3>{faqs.map(([q,a])=><details class="faq-detail"><summary>{q}</summary><p>{a}</p></details>)}</section><section class="three-tool-section" id="packing-deep-sources"><h3>Sources and further reading</h3><ul><li><a href="https://umrah.nusuk.sa/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Official Nusuk Umrah platform</a></li><li><a href="https://quran.com/2/158" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Quran 2:158</a></li><li><a href="https://quran.com/2/197" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Quran 2:197</a></li><li><a href="https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/saudi-arabia" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">UK travel advice for Saudi Arabia</a></li></ul><p class="small">Original educational material. An ingredient list, travel checklist or counter is not religious certification. Independent qualified scholarly review remains pending.</p></section></section>